# AP Workspace — required configuration reference
#
# This is NOT a real .env file the app loads — the Worker runtime has no
# .env support, and this project doesn't use one. This file exists purely
# to document, by name only, every piece of configuration the Worker
# needs, so nothing has to be reverse-engineered from source later.
#
# Configure the real values through the Cloudflare dashboard:
#   Worker → Settings → Bindings          (for DB)
#   Worker → Settings → Variables and Secrets   (for the two below)
# Never put real values in this file, in source, or in any committed file.

# D1 database binding name the Worker code expects (env.DB). Bind it to
# your D1 database (see worker/README.md) under this exact name.
DB=

# Bootstrap admin credentials — set these ONLY for the first deploy, as
# Worker secrets (never as a repo file, never in source). The Worker
# creates exactly one admin account from these the first time any
# /api/auth/* request runs and no admin exists yet in AP Database, then
# never touches them again (see maybeBootstrapAdmin in worker/src/index.js).
# Delete both secrets from the Worker once you've confirmed you can sign
# in — leaving them is safe (bootstrap is idempotent) but removing them
# means the Worker doesn't even query the database to check anymore.
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_USERNAME=
BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
